[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: One layer or two between the hooks and the DSL

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-DSL-LAYER-COUNT
TITLE: One layer or two between the hooks and the DSL
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: open
RETIRES_ON: The operator rules, or a construct is admitted that needs recursion or automatic graph-wide transitions.
STATEMENT: >>>
Is there ONE layer between the hook machinery (L2) and the DSL, or TWO? The
operator's rule: a second layer exists only if there is a forcing function at
the reasoning level -- a concern that cannot be thought about correctly while
also thinking about the other.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The spike found no such forcing function today. A condition is a total
function of one snapshot (always terminates, no effects); a hook has effects.
That justifies one piece of DATA between them -- the rule as JSON, riding in
the hook's own settings -- not a layer. Every Nix precedent studied (systemd
sugar, arion, git-hooks.nix) has exactly one intermediate. What WOULD earn a
second layer: recursion in conditions (multi-hop, repeat-until-stable) or
automatic graph-wide transitions, because termination and ordering then become
concerns of their own. Both are recommended out of scope, so the second layer
is unearned until one of them is admitted.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Brought to the operator 2026-08-29 as a card with the one-layer recommendation. DEFERRED: the operator is still brainstorming the semantic layer and does not want to rule while the destination is fuzzy. Stays open; the RETIRES_ON names the forcing functions (recursion in conditions, automatic graph-wide transitions) that would force it.
<<<
